#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD2004 expect=skipped domain=DM
#note "DELIBERATELY NO DTHFL COLUMN. Negative-comparison arm of the absent-column guard family: X != \"Y\" against a missing value normally FIRES, but the machine-emitted var_exists(\"DTHFL\") conjunct suppresses it -> no violation, with the rule executing. A submission that omits DTHFL entirely while recording DTHDTC is NOT reported by this rule. DTHFL is Expected in SDTMIG 3.4 DM (SD2004-F1); contrast the adapted invalid_empty_dthfl fixture in the same directory where an EMPTY flag fires. PLAN-retire-corpus-transforms phase 4: the rule now declares the gate variable in Requirements.Variables.All, so the absent column takes the auditable SKIP this scenario pins (Fix #330 remedy: a presence rule reports the absence once)."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset DM label="Demographics"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SUBJID  type=Char label="Subject Identifier for the Study"
col DTHDTC  type=Char label="Date/Time of Death"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1015 | 1015 | 2020-05-01
